<title>JAPAN: Japanese firms to build hot strip mill in China.</title>
<headline>Japanese firms to build hot strip mill in China.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Mitsubishi Corp said on Tuesday that it and five other Japanese firms had won an order to build a hot strip mill for the Anshan Iron and Steel Complex group in China.</p>
<p>The mill, which will make steel sheets, will have an annual production capacity of 3.5 million tonnes. Construction is expected to be completed in February 2000, a spokesman for the trading house said.</p>
<p>The Mitsubishi Corp spokesman declined to give the value of the order, but the business daily Nihon Keizai Shimbun said on Tuesday that it was estimated to be worth 40 billion yen.</p>
<p>The other five firms are Mitsubishi Heavy Industries Ltd, Mitsubishi Electric Corp, Ishikawajima-Harima Heavy Industries Co Ltd, Ube Industries Ltd and Sumitomo Metal Industries Ltd.</p>
</text>
